1
00:00:06,756 --> 00:00:08,757
- Hey, good morning!
- Morning.

2
00:00:08,758 --> 00:00:11,010
- What's good, everyone?
- Rise and shine.

3
00:00:11,011 --> 00:00:14,097
We gotta start the day off right.
Good morning, wassup?

4
00:00:18,643 --> 00:00:21,353
- He's a little too relaxed.
- Too what?

5
00:00:21,354 --> 00:00:22,856
- Excuse me.
- "Relaxed."

6
00:00:23,440 --> 00:00:25,899
- Will you stop?
- What? What happened now?

7
00:00:25,900 --> 00:00:27,568
- Seriously, guys.
- Hang on.

8
00:00:27,569 --> 00:00:28,902
Sorry to interrupt again,

9
00:00:28,903 --> 00:00:31,488
but there's another thing
I need to tell you all.

10
00:00:31,489 --> 00:00:32,614
KAZU-KUN (29)
HOST CLUB OWNER

11
00:00:32,615 --> 00:00:34,408
- Not this again.
- So…

12
00:00:34,409 --> 00:00:35,367
RURU (26)
MODEL

13
00:00:35,368 --> 00:00:38,162
Assun, do you remember
what you did late last night?

14
00:00:38,163 --> 00:00:40,414
Huh? I don't remember.

15
00:00:40,415 --> 00:00:42,124
ASSUN (30)
ENTREPRENEUR/HOSTESS

16
00:00:42,125 --> 00:00:45,920
Well, last night,
there was an incident where you got drunk

17
00:00:47,047 --> 00:00:49,006
and barged into the men's bedroom.

18
00:00:49,007 --> 00:00:50,049
- Seriously?
- What?

19
00:00:50,050 --> 00:00:51,800
- <i>What?</i>
- That's what happened.

20
00:00:51,801 --> 00:00:55,096
- No way. I don't remember.
- I was awake at the time.

21
00:00:57,474 --> 00:00:58,516
Hey.

22
00:00:59,768 --> 00:01:01,603
- <i>They're asleep.</i>
- Who is it?

23
00:01:02,937 --> 00:01:05,148
- Ma-kun.
- He's sleeping.

24
00:01:05,732 --> 00:01:06,566
Masaya.

25
00:01:07,776 --> 00:01:10,070
- No, I need to talk to him.
- Uh…

26
00:01:11,362 --> 00:01:12,530
- You can't do that.
- Wake him up.

27
00:01:14,032 --> 00:01:16,242
Sorry, but you need to leave the room.

28
00:01:18,369 --> 00:01:19,788
<i>Ah, so that was Leo.</i>

29
00:01:22,082 --> 00:01:24,625
To reiterate, in the hours after bedtime,

30
00:01:24,626 --> 00:01:28,796
both men and women are strictly prohibited
from entering each other's bedrooms.

31
00:01:28,797 --> 00:01:30,256
- Yes.
- That's the rule.

32
00:01:30,965 --> 00:01:33,884
As our school rules say,
no inappropriate relationships

33
00:01:33,885 --> 00:01:35,427
are allowed on campus.

34
00:01:35,428 --> 00:01:37,180
- Yes.
- It's clearly written down.

35
00:01:37,889 --> 00:01:41,892
Assun, you were suspended for one day
because of an alcohol-related issue.

36
00:01:41,893 --> 00:01:43,602
And on the exact day you returned…

37
00:01:43,603 --> 00:01:44,645
Mmm-hmm.

38
00:01:44,646 --> 00:01:47,107
…another alcohol-related incident
took place.

39
00:01:48,399 --> 00:01:50,527
We won't be taking
any disciplinary action.

40
00:01:51,611 --> 00:01:55,447
That said, we really urge you
to reflect on your actions.

41
00:01:55,448 --> 00:01:56,866
- Yes.
- That's how we feel.

42
00:01:57,992 --> 00:02:00,285
I'm sorry, everyone,
especially on the final day.

43
00:02:00,286 --> 00:02:01,496
It's okay, we're totally fine.

44
00:02:02,789 --> 00:02:05,541
You've got to be careful
with alcohol, okay, Asuka?

45
00:02:05,542 --> 00:02:06,417
- Yes.
- Behave yourself.

46
00:02:09,045 --> 00:02:12,298
This girl is not gonna shape up
unless someone teaches her a lesson.

47
00:02:14,050 --> 00:02:15,677
So, what would you do, Kazuma?

48
00:02:16,261 --> 00:02:17,262
I'd definitely…

49
00:02:18,138 --> 00:02:19,972
come down hard on her.

50
00:02:19,973 --> 00:02:24,894
Yeah, that makes sense.
Hmm… What am I gonna do?

51
00:02:34,821 --> 00:02:37,030
It's tricky when it comes to alcohol.

52
00:02:37,031 --> 00:02:39,992
In all honesty, I feel like
neither side is really wrong.

53
00:02:39,993 --> 00:02:40,993
- Hmm.
- Yeah, yeah.

54
00:02:40,994 --> 00:02:41,828
That's why…

55
00:02:42,328 --> 00:02:45,414
alcohol consumption
is one of the harder issues

56
00:02:45,415 --> 00:02:47,959
to find common ground on, I think.

57
00:03:00,972 --> 00:03:03,057
A YANKII DATING REALITY SHOW
WHERE LOVE LIVES ON THE EDGE

58
00:03:04,225 --> 00:03:06,143
RAPPER FROM SAGAMIHARA
SPITTING LYRICS OF PURE LOVE

59
00:03:06,144 --> 00:03:07,811
ARI

60
00:03:07,812 --> 00:03:09,855
KAWASAKI'S IT-GIRL HOSTESS
OUT TO FIND A REAL MAN

61
00:03:09,856 --> 00:03:11,023
HIKARU

62
00:03:11,024 --> 00:03:12,692
KYOTO BAR OWNER
GOING ALL-IN FOR HIS WOMAN

63
00:03:13,985 --> 00:03:15,694
NANIWA'S BARROOM BEAUTY
LOOKING FOR TRUE LOVE

64
00:03:15,695 --> 00:03:16,862
MARIRIN

65
00:03:16,863 --> 00:03:18,322
KURUME YANKII
WHO GREW UP BEHIND BARS

66
00:03:18,323 --> 00:03:19,449
BO

67
00:03:21,451 --> 00:03:23,410
EX-YAKUZA MMA FIGHTER
LOOKING FOR HIS RIDE-OR-DIE

68
00:03:23,411 --> 00:03:24,870
MA-KUN

69
00:03:24,871 --> 00:03:26,747
NAGOYA'S NO.1 HOSTESS
WHO PUTS MEN IN THEIR PLACE

70
00:03:26,748 --> 00:03:27,831
ASSUN

71
00:03:27,832 --> 00:03:29,291
FACE-TATTOOED STYLIST
WHO LOVES HARD

72
00:03:29,292 --> 00:03:30,751
TAI-CHAN

73
00:03:30,752 --> 00:03:32,044
AN HONEST MODEL
IN SEARCH OF LOVE

74
00:03:32,045 --> 00:03:33,129
RURU

75
00:03:37,050 --> 00:03:39,885
BRING ON THE FIGHTS
BRING ON THE LOVE

76
00:03:39,886 --> 00:03:41,094
NO FILTER KICKBOXER
FROM MIYAGI

77
00:03:41,095 --> 00:03:42,346
HA-CHAN

78
00:03:42,347 --> 00:03:43,597
EX-NO.1 HOST
CHASING TRUE LOVE

79
00:03:43,598 --> 00:03:44,599
KAZU-KUN

80
00:04:14,003 --> 00:04:15,672
<i>Tonight is the final night.</i>

81
00:04:16,464 --> 00:04:19,716
<i>Everyone, make up your mind
about your feelings</i>

82
00:04:19,717 --> 00:04:23,096
<i>and prepare for tomorrow's
graduation ceremony.</i>

83
00:04:24,430 --> 00:04:26,765
<i>Honestly, it doesn't feel like
the final day, does it?</i>

84
00:04:26,766 --> 00:04:28,183
- <i>Right.</i>
- <i>It doesn't.</i>

85
00:04:28,184 --> 00:04:30,560
<i>So much happened.
I seriously went through every emotion.</i>

86
00:04:30,561 --> 00:04:31,478
<i>Yeah.</i>

87
00:04:31,479 --> 00:04:33,773
- <i>Like a roller coaster.</i>
- <i>We cried, we laughed.</i>

88
00:04:34,440 --> 00:04:36,566
<i>If I had to use one word, it's "growth."</i>

89
00:04:36,567 --> 00:04:39,320
- <i>Fo' sho.</i>
- <i>That's cute.</i>

90
00:04:39,904 --> 00:04:40,988
<i>Nice growth.</i>

91
00:04:40,989 --> 00:04:42,614
<i>And what do we have in our hearts?</i>

92
00:04:42,615 --> 00:04:44,533
<i>Friendship!</i>

93
00:04:44,534 --> 00:04:47,661
<i>Wow, you finally turned into
a rapper too, Ma-kun. Finally!</i>

94
00:04:47,662 --> 00:04:49,998
- <i>A stocky-built rapper.</i>
- <i>Hey, don't call me stocky.</i>

95
00:04:54,794 --> 00:04:55,795
Here we go.

96
00:04:59,007 --> 00:05:00,674
- Want to sit?
- Yeah.

97
00:05:00,675 --> 00:05:02,719
- <i>Go, Maririn!</i>
- How are you feeling?

98
00:05:04,262 --> 00:05:05,638
Hmm…

99
00:05:06,681 --> 00:05:09,182
- So much has happened here.
- Yeah, seriously.

100
00:05:09,183 --> 00:05:10,475
TAI-CHAN (22)
HAIRSTYLIST

101
00:05:10,476 --> 00:05:11,852
MARIRIN (25)
BAR WORKER

102
00:05:11,853 --> 00:05:14,813
Having been able to grow together was one
of those things we can call love.

103
00:05:14,814 --> 00:05:16,274
- - Mmm.
- Yeah

104
00:05:19,694 --> 00:05:21,946
- Who should I confess to?
- Mmm.

105
00:05:22,488 --> 00:05:24,698
I feel like I'm the only indecisive one.

106
00:05:24,699 --> 00:05:26,700
Like, I still can't make up my mind
even in the end.

107
00:05:26,701 --> 00:05:27,535
Right.

108
00:05:28,578 --> 00:05:30,872
- Yeah.
- You have until the last second to think.

109
00:05:31,497 --> 00:05:33,457
Either way, I'm rooting for you.

110
00:05:33,458 --> 00:05:34,709
- Yeah.
- And I like you.

111
00:05:36,169 --> 00:05:38,588
- I accept every part of you.
- You do? Mmm.

112
00:05:41,591 --> 00:05:45,218
Even if I get rejected,
I feel like I'd be okay with that.

113
00:05:45,219 --> 00:05:49,139
But if there's even one person
in this entire world…

114
00:05:49,140 --> 00:05:51,767
who likes me or thinks I'm special,

115
00:05:51,768 --> 00:05:54,854
then I feel like
I can keep living my life positively.

116
00:05:58,274 --> 00:05:59,776
You pretty much made up your mind?

117
00:06:00,777 --> 00:06:02,444
- Hmm…
- Not yet?

118
00:06:02,445 --> 00:06:03,279
Not yet.

119
00:06:03,821 --> 00:06:05,030
I see.

120
00:06:05,031 --> 00:06:06,157
Another beautiful moon.

121
00:06:07,367 --> 00:06:08,284
It really is.

122
00:06:08,785 --> 00:06:10,577
They say the phrase
"the moon is beautiful"

123
00:06:10,578 --> 00:06:12,871
is the Japanese way
of saying "I love you."

124
00:06:12,872 --> 00:06:13,706
Oh, really?

125
00:06:15,625 --> 00:06:16,876
I want you and no one else.

126
00:06:18,044 --> 00:06:21,005
My feelings haven't changed
right up until the final day.

127
00:06:23,674 --> 00:06:24,758
BO (27)
COMMERCIAL PAINTER

128
00:06:24,759 --> 00:06:26,886
- Thank you for facing me head-on.
- No problem.

129
00:06:27,637 --> 00:06:31,057
But I also think it's amazing that
you made me want to face you head-on.

130
00:06:31,766 --> 00:06:32,642
- You think so?
- Yeah.

131
00:06:33,476 --> 00:06:37,355
Hmm. I guess when I like someone,
I want to pursue it all the way.

132
00:06:39,774 --> 00:06:41,943
Hmm.

133
00:06:43,152 --> 00:06:45,071
<i>Everyone's grown so much.</i>

134
00:06:45,738 --> 00:06:47,156
I don't want any regrets.

135
00:06:49,117 --> 00:06:50,076
True that.

136
00:06:52,203 --> 00:06:54,622
Ah, it's the bad boy. Here he comes.

137
00:06:55,706 --> 00:06:58,000
- What are you guys doing?
- What do you want, man?

138
00:06:58,501 --> 00:07:00,710
- You talking?
- It's fine, you can talk.

139
00:07:00,711 --> 00:07:02,921
Oh, wait, let me get my bag.

140
00:07:02,922 --> 00:07:04,756
Did you tell her
everything you wanted to, Bo?

141
00:07:04,757 --> 00:07:05,591
Yeah.

142
00:07:06,926 --> 00:07:09,594
- Then can I borrow Hikaru for a bit?
- I didn't ask but…

143
00:07:09,595 --> 00:07:13,056
- Mmm?
- <i>Oh, he's being bold.</i>

144
00:07:13,057 --> 00:07:13,891
Thank you.

145
00:07:15,560 --> 00:07:16,643
See ya.

146
00:07:16,644 --> 00:07:18,020
- Hey, Bo.
- Yeah.

147
00:07:23,067 --> 00:07:25,736
Well, these two weeks
were heavier than prison.

148
00:07:26,362 --> 00:07:27,279
Yeah.

149
00:07:27,280 --> 00:07:30,199
Facing other people means
facing yourself too, right?

150
00:07:30,741 --> 00:07:32,702
I never did that when I was in prison.

151
00:07:33,369 --> 00:07:35,079
But here, I faced 'em head-on.

152
00:07:36,456 --> 00:07:39,250
And through that,
I think I've grown as a person.

153
00:07:40,084 --> 00:07:40,918
Mmm.

154
00:07:41,711 --> 00:07:42,962
Given the way I am,

155
00:07:43,796 --> 00:07:46,507
I guess it comes down
to what the girls think of me.

156
00:07:57,101 --> 00:07:58,768
<i>What's he gonna say to her?</i>

157
00:07:58,769 --> 00:08:00,813
- Yo, Hikaru.
- Yo, yo.

158
00:08:01,481 --> 00:08:03,733
I went all in yesterday,
but it completely shattered me.

159
00:08:04,275 --> 00:08:06,861
- So you've been shattered twice?
- Yeah, you're right.

160
00:08:07,361 --> 00:08:09,446
I've probably been shattered
more than anyone here.

161
00:08:09,447 --> 00:08:11,657
- That's okay. That's growth.
- Mmm.

162
00:08:13,201 --> 00:08:15,995
I'm honestly really torn inside right now.

163
00:08:17,205 --> 00:08:19,456
Should I pick up
the shattered pieces of me

164
00:08:19,457 --> 00:08:21,626
and go charging full speed at Ruru again?

165
00:08:22,877 --> 00:08:24,754
Is that the right move? Or should…

166
00:08:26,380 --> 00:08:28,256
should I go to the person
who taught me a lot?

167
00:08:28,257 --> 00:08:29,175
That's me.

168
00:08:30,051 --> 00:08:31,510
"That's me"?

169
00:08:31,511 --> 00:08:33,428
You said it. Stop that.

170
00:08:33,429 --> 00:08:36,599
- So, am I just delusional?
- No, you're not delusional.

171
00:08:38,267 --> 00:08:42,020
It's you, Hikaru. You're the one
who taught me so many things.

172
00:08:42,021 --> 00:08:42,855
Mmm.

173
00:08:44,690 --> 00:08:46,191
I know I turned my back on you once

174
00:08:46,192 --> 00:08:48,861
and showed you
a seriously pathetic side of me.

175
00:08:50,154 --> 00:08:50,988
Mm…

176
00:08:52,365 --> 00:08:55,326
you've always been there,
somewhere in the back of my mind.

177
00:09:01,916 --> 00:09:03,292
I've never said this out loud before.

178
00:09:05,795 --> 00:09:06,629
Yeah.

179
00:09:10,341 --> 00:09:12,468
I just can't find the answer yet.

180
00:09:14,762 --> 00:09:18,391
Just how much this girl, Hikaru,
like, means to me.

181
00:09:19,934 --> 00:09:23,354
It feels like I finally realized
how deep my feelings for her go.

182
00:09:25,398 --> 00:09:28,609
As for Maririn, first of all,
she has a kind heart

183
00:09:29,944 --> 00:09:31,571
and is always very considerate.

184
00:09:32,738 --> 00:09:35,950
Whenever I was feeling down,
she was always the first to notice.

185
00:09:37,118 --> 00:09:39,202
I mean, should I go for her?

186
00:09:39,203 --> 00:09:41,998
Or should I pick up
the shattered pieces of myself again

187
00:09:43,499 --> 00:09:45,084
and give it a shot with Ruru…

188
00:09:46,460 --> 00:09:47,336
one last time?

189
00:09:48,504 --> 00:09:51,048
I really can't find an answer,
even within myself.

190
00:10:00,600 --> 00:10:03,143
- Bo was looking for you.
- Bo was looking for me?

191
00:10:03,144 --> 00:10:04,936
- Yeah.
- Bo!

192
00:10:04,937 --> 00:10:05,855
What do you want?

193
00:10:06,856 --> 00:10:08,232
- Bo!
- What do you want?

194
00:10:10,359 --> 00:10:12,277
Ari said you were looking for me.

195
00:10:12,278 --> 00:10:13,529
What? Ari said that?

196
00:10:14,614 --> 00:10:15,906
That guy.

197
00:10:17,116 --> 00:10:19,534
Wait, Bo, I'm coming up.
Hold on, stay right there.

198
00:10:19,535 --> 00:10:20,494
Don't come up here.

199
00:10:21,120 --> 00:10:22,955
Huh? What did you just say, punk?

200
00:10:24,874 --> 00:10:26,750
- Tired, huh?
- I am.

201
00:10:26,751 --> 00:10:27,585
Thanks, Bo.

202
00:10:28,419 --> 00:10:29,961
- For what?
- Huh?

203
00:10:29,962 --> 00:10:30,879
For what?

204
00:10:30,880 --> 00:10:34,634
- Mmm, well, you know, a guy like you--
- Don't go getting butterflies, dumbass!

205
00:10:42,558 --> 00:10:44,852
- That's just who I am, okay?
- Oh, I know that already.

206
00:10:46,604 --> 00:10:48,772
It's just so dumb, you know.

207
00:10:48,773 --> 00:10:51,399
Jo-- Oops, I just called you "Jo."

208
00:10:51,400 --> 00:10:53,443
You love to provoke people.

209
00:10:53,444 --> 00:10:55,362
I can't help it. It's just who I am.

210
00:10:55,363 --> 00:10:56,696
- I know that.
- Mmm.

211
00:10:56,697 --> 00:10:58,990
But to be honest, I feel relaxed with you.

212
00:10:58,991 --> 00:11:00,409
Yeah, right.

213
00:11:01,327 --> 00:11:03,370
Don't get butterflies now!

214
00:11:03,371 --> 00:11:04,871
<i>Look at his face! Right?</i>

215
00:11:04,872 --> 00:11:06,581
- <i>I know.</i>
- <i>Only with Ha-chan.</i>

216
00:11:06,582 --> 00:11:08,792
<i>What kind of game is this?</i>

217
00:11:08,793 --> 00:11:10,835
- This girl is dangerous, for real!
- Did that hurt?

218
00:11:10,836 --> 00:11:12,879
Come on, this isn't <i>Mad Max.</i>

219
00:11:12,880 --> 00:11:14,757
Seriously.
She's not supposed to whack him.

220
00:11:15,341 --> 00:11:16,217
Sorry.

221
00:11:17,176 --> 00:11:18,010
Yeah.

222
00:11:18,803 --> 00:11:20,429
- Well…
- What?

223
00:11:22,932 --> 00:11:26,101
Don't you think making friends is
way easier than finding a girlfriend?

224
00:11:26,102 --> 00:11:27,435
HA-CHAN (27)
FIGHTER/SPORTS TRAINER

225
00:11:27,436 --> 00:11:29,689
I totally agree.
Being here has made me realize

226
00:11:30,648 --> 00:11:32,232
how much I suck at romance

227
00:11:32,233 --> 00:11:34,442
- all over again.
- Yeah, you suck at it.

228
00:11:34,443 --> 00:11:36,611
- Earlier, I-- Huh?
- "Huh?"

229
00:11:36,612 --> 00:11:40,782
Listen, why do you diss me
while I'm still talking?

230
00:11:40,783 --> 00:11:42,283
That's not very polite.

231
00:11:42,284 --> 00:11:45,078
Um, I'm bad at serious conversations.

232
00:11:45,079 --> 00:11:47,163
'Cause your face is already a joke?

233
00:11:47,164 --> 00:11:49,125
Exactly.

234
00:11:51,711 --> 00:11:55,672
It's like his kindness works
in ways you can't even see.

235
00:11:55,673 --> 00:11:59,301
He has so many little, subtle acts
of kindness like that.

236
00:12:00,136 --> 00:12:02,470
So, when I think

237
00:12:02,471 --> 00:12:06,934
and ask myself for real who's the best guy
I want for my boyfriend,

238
00:12:08,060 --> 00:12:09,102
I think it's Bo.

239
00:12:09,103 --> 00:12:10,438
It's just-- Well…

240
00:12:11,605 --> 00:12:15,567
Maybe I've never really made
the first move in romance before,

241
00:12:15,568 --> 00:12:18,862
especially when I wasn't drinking
or anything like that.

242
00:12:18,863 --> 00:12:21,031
But that's not how things work here.

243
00:12:22,616 --> 00:12:25,243
I feel like I'm working up all my courage

244
00:12:25,244 --> 00:12:28,539
to face the truth
and choose Bo. Right now.

245
00:12:37,631 --> 00:12:40,760
- How's it going?
- How's it going? Mm…

246
00:12:41,844 --> 00:12:43,846
- Well, nothing has changed for me.
- Yeah.

247
00:12:44,513 --> 00:12:46,806
My feelings haven't changed at all.

248
00:12:46,807 --> 00:12:47,641
Mmm,

249
00:12:48,726 --> 00:12:50,269
I'm going to confess to you tomorrow.

250
00:12:53,773 --> 00:12:55,065
- Yeah.
- Mmm.

251
00:12:58,235 --> 00:12:59,861
- But still, um…
- But what?

252
00:12:59,862 --> 00:13:02,531
My resolve is set.
I already have my answer.

253
00:13:03,741 --> 00:13:05,033
That's scary.

254
00:13:05,034 --> 00:13:07,285
We've barely talked,
and you're already saying that?

255
00:13:07,286 --> 00:13:08,912
I know!

256
00:13:08,913 --> 00:13:10,538
You're making me look like I got rejected.

257
00:13:10,539 --> 00:13:12,499
We've only talked for, like, two minutes,

258
00:13:12,500 --> 00:13:14,709
and you're already like,
"I've made up my mind."

259
00:13:14,710 --> 00:13:15,710
MAXIMUM MANLINESS!

260
00:13:15,711 --> 00:13:17,921
Seriously, that overnight trip
was intense.

261
00:13:17,922 --> 00:13:20,674
What decided it?
What made you think, "He is the one"?

262
00:13:21,467 --> 00:13:23,010
Hmm…

263
00:13:25,054 --> 00:13:26,346
- I decided…
- Yeah?

264
00:13:26,347 --> 00:13:30,266
I decided to stay true
to my own feelings, I guess.

265
00:13:30,267 --> 00:13:32,685
Ah, so no specific thing,
but looking at the whole picture?

266
00:13:32,686 --> 00:13:33,771
Exactly.

267
00:13:35,940 --> 00:13:37,233
How will it shake out?

268
00:13:39,360 --> 00:13:41,445
But she said her resolve was set.

269
00:13:43,239 --> 00:13:45,741
Well, whatever her resolve may be…

270
00:13:48,077 --> 00:13:49,620
I'll support her decision.

271
00:13:51,747 --> 00:13:53,082
And if she chooses me,

272
00:13:54,625 --> 00:13:56,585
I'll face her with everything I've got.

273
00:13:58,295 --> 00:13:59,380
How should I put it?

274
00:14:00,422 --> 00:14:02,841
The fact that I've been able to…

275
00:14:02,842 --> 00:14:03,758
Mmm.

276
00:14:03,759 --> 00:14:06,762
…face you this seriously, to be so honest…

277
00:14:08,889 --> 00:14:10,515
makes me a little surprised at myself.

278
00:14:10,516 --> 00:14:11,767
- Mmm.
- Yeah.

279
00:14:12,351 --> 00:14:15,144
From the bottom of my heart,
I'm really glad I met you, Ruru.

280
00:14:15,145 --> 00:14:15,980
Mmm.

281
00:14:17,273 --> 00:14:18,607
I don't think I've ever…

282
00:14:21,151 --> 00:14:23,444
fell for someone
this much before, I mean it.

283
00:14:23,445 --> 00:14:25,447
Mmm. But for me too.

284
00:14:26,198 --> 00:14:27,032
It's like,

285
00:14:27,908 --> 00:14:31,495
after meeting you, and hearing the words
that came out of your mouth…

286
00:14:32,246 --> 00:14:34,623
I'd never had anyone
say those things to me.

287
00:14:36,500 --> 00:14:38,877
It's just… It's all new.

288
00:14:38,878 --> 00:14:41,379
I'd never thought about someone
this much before.

289
00:14:41,380 --> 00:14:42,339
Yeah, I get it.

290
00:14:43,173 --> 00:14:46,342
And honestly,
I had so much fun with you here.

291
00:14:46,343 --> 00:14:48,095
- For real.
- Yeah. Same here.

292
00:14:48,596 --> 00:14:50,763
You're always cracking me up, Leo.

293
00:14:50,764 --> 00:14:52,474
It just comes naturally.

294
00:14:53,100 --> 00:14:55,227
- You can be your true self from now on.
- Yeah.

295
00:14:56,979 --> 00:14:59,355
I'm being my true self
right now, talking to you.

296
00:14:59,356 --> 00:15:00,357
Yeah, yeah.

297
00:15:03,277 --> 00:15:05,778
And you're the one
who made me feel this way,

298
00:15:05,779 --> 00:15:08,239
you're the one
who helped me grow like this.

299
00:15:08,240 --> 00:15:09,158
Yeah.

300
00:15:10,242 --> 00:15:11,410
Seriously…

301
00:15:12,995 --> 00:15:14,538
for these past two weeks,

302
00:15:15,539 --> 00:15:18,834
thank you for always telling me
how you feel, with such passion.

303
00:15:19,335 --> 00:15:21,587
No problem at all.
I just want to be honest with you.

304
00:15:25,174 --> 00:15:28,928
But you know what? I thought
my resolve was set until just now.

305
00:15:30,596 --> 00:15:32,932
Sorry, but to be honest,
I'm completely torn.

306
00:15:33,682 --> 00:15:34,558
Really.

307
00:15:36,852 --> 00:15:39,313
I couldn't find the answer
this whole time.

308
00:15:40,147 --> 00:15:43,316
But now, I think I finally know
what it feels like to be in love.

309
00:15:43,317 --> 00:15:44,692
I can actually feel it, right now.

310
00:15:44,693 --> 00:15:45,694
<i>What?</i>

311
00:15:47,154 --> 00:15:49,281
No matter how this turns out,

312
00:15:50,658 --> 00:15:51,742
I have no regrets.

313
00:15:52,993 --> 00:15:55,913
When I confess tomorrow,
I want to do it with confidence.

314
00:15:59,291 --> 00:16:00,584
I'll tell her how I feel…

315
00:16:02,294 --> 00:16:05,005
put it all out there, through my words

316
00:16:06,340 --> 00:16:07,924
and my emotions.

317
00:16:07,925 --> 00:16:09,468
That's what I want to do.

318
00:16:23,482 --> 00:16:25,901
- I have a lesson I've learned for myself.
- Mmm.

319
00:16:26,527 --> 00:16:27,902
When things seem to be going well,

320
00:16:27,903 --> 00:16:29,946
I think it's because someone
is putting up with me.

321
00:16:29,947 --> 00:16:30,781
Mmm.

322
00:16:31,699 --> 00:16:32,658
That makes sense.

323
00:16:33,367 --> 00:16:36,703
Asuka, let me tell you, I'm the type
of person who puts up with things

324
00:16:36,704 --> 00:16:38,997
until I absolutely can't anymore.

325
00:16:38,998 --> 00:16:40,290
- Yeah, I figured.
- Yeah.

326
00:16:40,958 --> 00:16:43,627
- I don't say anything.
- I want you to stop doing that.

327
00:16:44,837 --> 00:16:47,171
- The reason behind all my past breakups…
- Yeah?

328
00:16:47,172 --> 00:16:50,383
…is because I'd put up with everything
and said nothing for too long--

329
00:16:50,384 --> 00:16:53,886
- That's the worst thing you can do.
- And at the very end, boom. I just snap.

330
00:16:53,887 --> 00:16:55,930
- You must know that.
- Really. I know.

331
00:16:55,931 --> 00:16:58,142
- I hit my limit eventually, you know?
- Yeah.

332
00:17:00,477 --> 00:17:01,854
Yeah, that's just how I am.

333
00:17:08,235 --> 00:17:12,197
Seriously, I have so many things
I want to tell you, of course.

334
00:17:12,865 --> 00:17:13,699
Mmm.

335
00:17:14,450 --> 00:17:15,367
Mmm.

336
00:17:16,535 --> 00:17:18,245
Um, you know…

337
00:17:20,122 --> 00:17:21,832
- when I was coming here…
- Mmm?

338
00:17:22,499 --> 00:17:25,209
I was so nervous
because of what happened with my ex.

339
00:17:25,210 --> 00:17:28,087
And I still hadn't completely
gotten over her when I arrived.

340
00:17:28,088 --> 00:17:29,005
Mmm-hmm.

341
00:17:29,006 --> 00:17:31,924
I thought there probably
wouldn't be anyone here for me

342
00:17:31,925 --> 00:17:34,135
who could take her place.

343
00:17:34,136 --> 00:17:37,056
But I did come here
with this tiny bit of hope,

344
00:17:37,890 --> 00:17:40,308
wishing that maybe I could find someone

345
00:17:40,309 --> 00:17:42,894
who would show up
and be what she was for me.

346
00:17:42,895 --> 00:17:43,771
Yeah.

347
00:17:44,354 --> 00:17:46,648
And if that person were to show up,

348
00:17:47,566 --> 00:17:48,692
I wanted to…

349
00:17:49,777 --> 00:17:52,361
write an original song for her
and confess my feelings through it.

350
00:17:52,362 --> 00:17:53,197
Mmm.

351
00:17:54,406 --> 00:17:56,866
So, I actually wrote you
a brand-new track,

352
00:17:56,867 --> 00:17:58,367
you know, some new shit,

353
00:17:58,368 --> 00:18:00,787
so I was wondering
if it would be all right

354
00:18:00,788 --> 00:18:02,080
if I perform it right now?

355
00:18:02,081 --> 00:18:02,998
Oh, okay.

356
00:18:06,418 --> 00:18:08,336
This is totally weird, right?

357
00:18:08,337 --> 00:18:10,088
- Ready?
- Yeah, I'm ready.

358
00:18:10,089 --> 00:18:11,131
Here goes.

359
00:18:13,675 --> 00:18:14,718
Stop giggling.

360
00:18:15,719 --> 00:18:16,720
<i>Yeah, uh</i>

361
00:18:18,722 --> 00:18:20,516
<i>Yeah, uh, yeah</i>

362
00:18:22,559 --> 00:18:25,728
<i>Met in Okinawa, At the entrance ceremony</i>

363
00:18:25,729 --> 00:18:27,980
<i>We both come from Kanagawa City</i>

364
00:18:27,981 --> 00:18:30,775
<i>Blonde hair, with that cute
Snaggletooth smile</i>

365
00:18:30,776 --> 00:18:33,653
<i>You seriously lit up the whole aisle</i>

366
00:18:33,654 --> 00:18:36,114
<i>Like a bright star,
You were shining true</i>

367
00:18:36,115 --> 00:18:38,741
<i>You told me that your name's "Hikaru"</i>

368
00:18:38,742 --> 00:18:40,868
<i>No doubt in my mind,
You're my MVP</i>

369
00:18:40,869 --> 00:18:43,996
<i>Something about you,
You were one of a kind</i>

370
00:18:43,997 --> 00:18:45,998
<i>Hikaru, you're my only one</i>

371
00:18:45,999 --> 00:18:48,584
<i>Even when we fight,
Don't say that we're done</i>

372
00:18:48,585 --> 00:18:51,379
<i>If you're feeling down,
I'll write you a letter</i>

373
00:18:51,380 --> 00:18:53,965
<i>I'll even clean the room,
If it makes you feel better</i>

374
00:18:53,966 --> 00:18:56,551
<i>Whatever comes our way
I'll be by your side</i>

375
00:18:56,552 --> 00:18:59,220
<i>"Hika-Ari" forever,
We got nothing to hide</i>

376
00:18:59,221 --> 00:19:02,098
<i>Hikaru, I'll be the one
Who makes you smile</i>

377
00:19:02,099 --> 00:19:05,060
<i>So stay right by my side,
Every step, every mile</i>

378
00:19:08,147 --> 00:19:11,149
- Wassup! Wassup!
- Wassup! Wassup!

379
00:19:11,150 --> 00:19:13,610
Look at you, you're a real-deal rapper.

380
00:19:14,278 --> 00:19:17,155
Yeah. Well, I wrote it all down.
Just, you know…

381
00:19:17,156 --> 00:19:19,699
- That hit me hard. That's cheating.
- Cheating?

382
00:19:19,700 --> 00:19:21,326
Can you stand up for a second?

383
00:19:23,495 --> 00:19:24,413
Look, I mean,

384
00:19:25,247 --> 00:19:27,082
this is how I truly feel.

385
00:19:27,791 --> 00:19:28,792
When I'm rapping,

386
00:19:29,751 --> 00:19:31,752
I don't lie. For real.

387
00:19:31,753 --> 00:19:33,046
Hikaru, I'm…

388
00:19:34,464 --> 00:19:36,299
I'm really in love with you.

389
00:19:36,300 --> 00:19:37,967
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

390
00:19:37,968 --> 00:19:39,385
- Yeah.
- For meeting me.

391
00:19:39,386 --> 00:19:40,429
Thank you.

392
00:19:43,682 --> 00:19:47,978
Well, my ex put a love spell on me,
but it's completely broken now.

393
00:19:48,979 --> 00:19:51,940
I'm already looking toward
the next person.

394
00:19:52,733 --> 00:19:55,026
I have no regrets.
I did everything I could.

395
00:19:55,027 --> 00:19:58,864
Over these past two weeks,
I know I truly gave everything I could.

396
00:19:59,531 --> 00:20:02,910
I can't do any more than this.
I have no regrets at all.

397
00:20:32,856 --> 00:20:35,150
When I think about
whether I like him or not…

398
00:20:38,737 --> 00:20:39,780
I don't know.

399
00:20:44,660 --> 00:20:45,744
Hmm…

400
00:20:49,498 --> 00:20:53,168
Well, it's gonna be Asuka tomorrow.
Of course. Asuka for sure.

401
00:20:53,919 --> 00:20:54,920
I'll confess to her.

402
00:20:56,421 --> 00:20:57,923
I can picture a future with her.

403
00:20:58,674 --> 00:21:00,509
That's why I want
to leave this place with her.

404
00:21:01,051 --> 00:21:04,638
Love is great, isn't it?
It's so warm. It really is.

405
00:21:06,265 --> 00:21:08,850
Receiving it and giving it. Both ways.

406
00:21:09,518 --> 00:21:10,394
Love is great.

407
00:21:12,229 --> 00:21:16,108
Like, honestly,
the more seriously I think about it…

408
00:21:18,694 --> 00:21:20,946
the more I wonder
if I'm really good enough for him,

409
00:21:21,947 --> 00:21:23,740
or if things would actually work
between us.

410
00:21:25,534 --> 00:21:28,495
And then, of course,
there's the alcohol thing.

411
00:21:29,871 --> 00:21:33,333
I'm worried he'll end up
putting up with it without telling me.

412
00:21:35,627 --> 00:21:38,588
Well, I definitely don't want
to put him through that.

413
00:21:41,883 --> 00:21:44,761
So, maybe we're better off
not ending up together.

414
00:22:16,877 --> 00:22:18,586
Whether we have regrets or not,

415
00:22:18,587 --> 00:22:19,795
- this is ending.
- Yeah.

416
00:22:19,796 --> 00:22:24,176
Coming here, what I learned most
was the love I received from you all.

417
00:22:25,302 --> 00:22:26,845
I was able to change a lot.

418
00:22:27,888 --> 00:22:30,431
I'm excited for tomorrow.
I'm sad, but excited too.

419
00:22:30,432 --> 00:22:31,349
Right.

420
00:22:31,350 --> 00:22:34,060
It was also a time for me
to reflect on my own flaws.

421
00:22:34,061 --> 00:22:35,311
- That's exactly it.
- Yeah.

422
00:22:35,312 --> 00:22:38,397
If I hadn't come here, I would've
stayed fine living with all of my flaws.

423
00:22:38,398 --> 00:22:40,941
Yeah, I didn't even mind
having them before.

424
00:22:40,942 --> 00:22:42,693
I thought about my past too.

425
00:22:42,694 --> 00:22:44,904
About the way
I've lived my life up until now.

426
00:22:44,905 --> 00:22:46,489
Yeah, yeah. I know.

427
00:22:46,490 --> 00:22:49,033
We came for romance,
but we learned so much more than that.

428
00:22:49,034 --> 00:22:50,284
- Yeah.
- So true.

429
00:22:50,285 --> 00:22:52,161
It's kind of love
in a broader sense, you know?

430
00:22:52,162 --> 00:22:54,373
- Yeah, exactly.
- Not just romantic love,

431
00:22:54,956 --> 00:22:56,583
- but love for our parents too.
- Yeah.

432
00:22:57,459 --> 00:22:59,795
- Maybe this is what <i>Badly In Love</i> is.
- Yeah.

433
00:23:01,338 --> 00:23:03,255
- Shall we huddle up?
- Shall we?

434
00:23:03,256 --> 00:23:04,465
Let's do it.

435
00:23:04,466 --> 00:23:07,260
Let's give it our all tomorrow
and tell them how we feel.

436
00:23:11,181 --> 00:23:12,765
- <i>So touching.</i>
- Here we go.

437
00:23:12,766 --> 00:23:13,974
Ready? And…

438
00:23:13,975 --> 00:23:17,311
<i>Badly In Love</i> is the best!

439
00:23:17,312 --> 00:23:18,813
We're family!

440
00:23:18,814 --> 00:23:20,564
- I really love you guys!
- Thank you.

441
00:23:20,565 --> 00:23:22,441
- I love you.
- Thanks a million.

442
00:23:22,442 --> 00:23:24,360
Yeah, me too, thanks a million.

443
00:23:24,361 --> 00:23:26,237
- Seriously, thank you.
- We're a family.

444
00:23:26,238 --> 00:23:27,322
We really are a family.

445
00:23:31,159 --> 00:23:33,369
Guys, thank you all for meeting me.

446
00:23:33,370 --> 00:23:35,037
Thank you.

447
00:23:35,038 --> 00:23:36,081
Thank you, everyone.

448
00:23:36,873 --> 00:23:37,957
- Mmm.
- Thank you.

449
00:23:37,958 --> 00:23:39,708
Tomorrow, let's make sure

450
00:23:39,709 --> 00:23:42,504
we all give it everything we've got,
with no regrets.

451
00:23:43,296 --> 00:23:46,173
Yeah, let's go for it
and make it the best day ever.

452
00:23:46,174 --> 00:23:49,136
I'm really glad I came here
and got to meet you guys.

453
00:23:49,719 --> 00:23:52,264
For me, I feel like
I've found true friendship.

454
00:23:53,348 --> 00:23:54,890
It's been real, guys. Seriously.

455
00:23:54,891 --> 00:23:57,018
This is gonna keep me going for life.

456
00:23:58,728 --> 00:24:01,273
This bond we shared here, all of it.

457
00:24:03,817 --> 00:24:05,569
I'm not afraid of anything anymore.

458
00:24:15,704 --> 00:24:17,955
- I don't want this to end.
- Me neither.

459
00:24:17,956 --> 00:24:20,416
But it's not gonna end for us,
even after we leave here.

460
00:24:20,417 --> 00:24:21,251
Right.

461
00:24:22,210 --> 00:24:24,628
We were able to meet,
thanks to this opportunity.

462
00:24:24,629 --> 00:24:26,006
- Right?
- Damn right.

463
00:24:39,978 --> 00:24:43,063
I love every one of you.
Let's bring our A-game tomorrow!

464
00:24:43,064 --> 00:24:45,150
Let's go!

465
00:24:48,612 --> 00:24:50,863
So, here we are at last.

466
00:24:50,864 --> 00:24:53,073
That's what a dating show
is supposed to be!

467
00:24:53,074 --> 00:24:54,533
Yes.

468
00:24:54,534 --> 00:24:57,077
We had to wait until the final episode…

469
00:24:57,078 --> 00:24:59,246
- but it happened.
- Thank you for your patience.

470
00:24:59,247 --> 00:25:03,125
And then Tai-chan, on the day
before the confession, of all days…

471
00:25:03,126 --> 00:25:04,084
Mmm.

472
00:25:04,085 --> 00:25:06,420
…started bringing up Hikaru
all over again.

473
00:25:06,421 --> 00:25:07,838
Mmm.

474
00:25:07,839 --> 00:25:11,634
- What's going on with Tai-chan?
- Jeez, Tai-chan is just so wishy-washy.

475
00:25:11,635 --> 00:25:14,887
Tai-chan… But I honestly thought
he should just go with Maririn.

476
00:25:14,888 --> 00:25:17,098
- Exactly.
- Since she's been coming onto him hard.

477
00:25:17,682 --> 00:25:19,141
I wonder who Tai-chan will pick.

478
00:25:19,142 --> 00:25:20,477
- I have no idea.
- Right.

479
00:25:21,061 --> 00:25:23,438
Meanwhile, Bo has feelings for Hikaru,

480
00:25:24,314 --> 00:25:27,149
but Ha-chan declared
she would confess her feelings to Bo.

481
00:25:27,150 --> 00:25:28,275
- Oh, right!
- Yep.

482
00:25:28,276 --> 00:25:30,945
All three of us agree that Bo and Ha-chan
are good together.

483
00:25:30,946 --> 00:25:31,862
- Right.
- Mmm.

484
00:25:31,863 --> 00:25:35,449
Ha-chan's the only one
Bo lets his guard down around, isn't she?

485
00:25:35,450 --> 00:25:36,992
- That's true. He does.
- Right?

486
00:25:36,993 --> 00:25:39,912
Ha-chan's really the only one
he shows his face to.

487
00:25:39,913 --> 00:25:41,705
But overall, everyone's faces

488
00:25:41,706 --> 00:25:43,541
- have really changed for the better.
- They have.

489
00:25:43,542 --> 00:25:44,959
- Yeah.
- Mmm.

490
00:25:44,960 --> 00:25:46,544
By the way, in this season,

491
00:25:46,545 --> 00:25:48,087
- the women can confess too.
- Yes!

492
00:25:48,088 --> 00:25:49,088
Eh?

493
00:25:49,089 --> 00:25:51,632
I've been thinking about that
this whole time.

494
00:25:51,633 --> 00:25:54,843
- Oh, really? You thought about it?
- I was like, "Let the women confess too!"

495
00:25:54,844 --> 00:25:56,804
- Wow! It's happening.
- That's what I thought.

496
00:25:56,805 --> 00:26:00,183
BRING ON THE LOVE
GRADUATION

497
00:26:06,773 --> 00:26:08,817
CONGRATULATIONS

498
00:26:19,744 --> 00:26:24,331
ASSUN

499
00:26:24,332 --> 00:26:29,670
MARIRIN

500
00:26:29,671 --> 00:26:35,134
HIKARU

501
00:26:35,135 --> 00:26:41,515
RURU

502
00:26:41,516 --> 00:26:48,064
HA-CHAN

503
00:27:44,204 --> 00:27:48,624
MA-KUN

504
00:27:48,625 --> 00:27:53,755
BO

505
00:27:58,551 --> 00:28:03,764
TAI-CHAN

506
00:28:03,765 --> 00:28:08,102
ARI

507
00:28:08,103 --> 00:28:12,774
KAZU-KUN

508
00:28:41,886 --> 00:28:45,097
<i>Everyone, we will now begin
the graduation ceremony.</i>

509
00:28:45,098 --> 00:28:46,223
GRADUATION

510
00:28:46,224 --> 00:28:49,393
<i>When your name is called,
please step forward,</i>

511
00:28:49,394 --> 00:28:52,354
<i>call the person you have feelings for,</i>

512
00:28:52,355 --> 00:28:54,524
<i>and confess your feelings to them.</i>

513
00:28:55,692 --> 00:28:58,235
<i>If you wish to object, please come forward</i>

514
00:28:58,236 --> 00:29:00,029
<i>and make your own confession.</i>

515
00:29:02,031 --> 00:29:02,949
<i>First up…</i>

516
00:29:05,201 --> 00:29:06,410
<i>Ma-kun.</i>

517
00:29:06,411 --> 00:29:07,287
All right!

518
00:29:07,871 --> 00:29:09,497
- Good luck.
- Thanks.

519
00:29:16,379 --> 00:29:18,797
Well, during our time here,

520
00:29:18,798 --> 00:29:20,215
a lot happened.

521
00:29:20,216 --> 00:29:24,094
But I learned so many things
and I learned them in my own way.

522
00:29:24,095 --> 00:29:27,348
And even after this is over,
they'll live on inside me.

523
00:29:27,932 --> 00:29:31,143
When my time comes, I know
I'll look back on this very moment.

524
00:29:31,144 --> 00:29:32,520
Thank you, guys, so much.

525
00:29:34,022 --> 00:29:36,566
The one I want to confess to is Asuka.

526
00:29:37,484 --> 00:29:38,735
- Come on up.
- Yes.

527
00:29:58,671 --> 00:30:00,839
Well, Asuka, I'm sure you already know,

528
00:30:00,840 --> 00:30:05,093
but from the moment I saw you,
everything about you was exactly my type.

529
00:30:05,094 --> 00:30:07,387
The more I knew you,
the more I fell for you.

530
00:30:07,388 --> 00:30:09,057
We did see you make mistakes,

531
00:30:09,724 --> 00:30:12,101
but you owned up to them, apologized.

532
00:30:12,811 --> 00:30:13,770
I thought that was cool.

533
00:30:14,813 --> 00:30:19,316
I'm still immature too
and still a work-in-progress as a man,

534
00:30:19,317 --> 00:30:21,777
but I swear I'll become
a real man one day.

535
00:30:21,778 --> 00:30:23,363
So, let's leave here together.

536
00:30:30,036 --> 00:30:30,870
Hmm.

537
00:30:33,790 --> 00:30:36,334
I really respect
that straightforward side of you

538
00:30:36,835 --> 00:30:40,296
and how incredibly unshakable
your inner core is.

539
00:30:42,882 --> 00:30:44,759
You're like, "I am who I am."

540
00:30:45,260 --> 00:30:48,638
I don't know if that makes things easier
or harder for you, though.

541
00:30:50,598 --> 00:30:54,185
Um, you can be awkward and straightforward
but deeply caring.

542
00:30:56,354 --> 00:30:57,397
And I like you.

543
00:31:02,902 --> 00:31:06,364
And, I think we'll have
a lot of challenges ahead.

544
00:31:08,408 --> 00:31:10,325
But let's get through them…

545
00:31:10,326 --> 00:31:11,160
together.

546
00:31:11,953 --> 00:31:13,413
I look forward to being with you.

547
00:31:16,749 --> 00:31:20,128
Wassup!

548
00:31:21,379 --> 00:31:24,464
Pow, pow, pow, pow, pow!

549
00:31:24,465 --> 00:31:28,177
- All right!
- Oh, yay! Oh!

550
00:31:29,012 --> 00:31:30,555
- Yeah!
- Wassup!

551
00:31:31,055 --> 00:31:33,557
- I'm about to cry.
- Wow, oh, my God. I'm gonna cry too.

552
00:31:33,558 --> 00:31:34,809
I can feel the tears.

553
00:31:35,435 --> 00:31:37,145
I feel like I just saw a wedding.

554
00:31:47,071 --> 00:31:48,364
<i>Next up is…</i>

555
00:31:50,241 --> 00:31:51,450
<i>Ha-chan.</i>

556
00:31:51,451 --> 00:31:53,118
<i>Oh, nice.</i>

557
00:31:53,119 --> 00:31:54,494
<i>- Go for it, Ha-chan.</i>
- Yes.

558
00:31:54,495 --> 00:31:55,622
<i>You got this, Ha-chan!</i>

559
00:31:56,664 --> 00:31:58,499
<i>It's her first-ever confession.</i>

560
00:32:03,504 --> 00:32:04,339
Um…

561
00:32:05,924 --> 00:32:08,676
First of all, when I joined
as the transfer student,

562
00:32:09,636 --> 00:32:13,306
I realize I probably didn't make
the best first impression.

563
00:32:15,183 --> 00:32:16,225
But even so…

564
00:32:17,727 --> 00:32:18,978
I was able to…

565
00:32:20,313 --> 00:32:21,564
become part of the group.

566
00:32:22,649 --> 00:32:24,943
I can say this
from the bottom of my heart now.

567
00:32:27,320 --> 00:32:28,154
Mm…

568
00:32:30,698 --> 00:32:34,327
The guy I want to confess
my feelings to is…

569
00:32:35,078 --> 00:32:35,912
Bo.

570
00:32:36,704 --> 00:32:37,705
Please come on up.

571
00:32:39,999 --> 00:32:41,000
Okay.

572
00:32:54,889 --> 00:32:56,265
I'm seriously nervous.

573
00:32:58,267 --> 00:32:59,811
So, to start out…

574
00:33:01,020 --> 00:33:03,398
when I was first trying to fit in,

575
00:33:05,233 --> 00:33:08,027
I said some rude things to you,
because I was drunk.

576
00:33:09,821 --> 00:33:14,325
But even when I was drunk,
you were able to, well,

577
00:33:15,326 --> 00:33:16,160
like…

578
00:33:16,744 --> 00:33:18,413
handle it in your own way.

579
00:33:19,872 --> 00:33:20,957
I really thought so.

580
00:33:24,419 --> 00:33:27,005
And as things went on with you…

581
00:33:28,214 --> 00:33:29,756
I guess since that night,

582
00:33:29,757 --> 00:33:33,761
we started talking and joking around
with each other a lot.

583
00:33:34,470 --> 00:33:35,972
I started noticing…

584
00:33:39,517 --> 00:33:42,645
things like how you are
with your subtle kindness.

585
00:33:45,857 --> 00:33:48,484
I'd like to learn more things
like that about you.

586
00:33:49,777 --> 00:33:51,446
That's simply how I feel.

587
00:33:52,321 --> 00:33:54,031
I hope you'll accept my feelings

588
00:33:54,032 --> 00:33:56,451
with the same kindness
you've always shown me.

589
00:34:02,832 --> 00:34:03,791
I'm sorry.

590
00:34:04,709 --> 00:34:06,460
I like someone else, so I can't.

591
00:34:06,461 --> 00:34:07,836
Yeah. I knew that.

592
00:34:07,837 --> 00:34:09,547
- Thank you.
- Thank you, though.

593
00:34:22,894 --> 00:34:24,353
- I tried my best.
- Mmm.

594
00:34:25,605 --> 00:34:26,939
- Good job.
- Yeah.

595
00:34:27,440 --> 00:34:28,690
Oh, she did well.

596
00:34:28,691 --> 00:34:30,358
- Ruru is so sweet.
- She was brave.

597
00:34:30,359 --> 00:34:31,276
She was.

598
00:34:31,277 --> 00:34:32,611
- She was so cool.
- Yeah.

599
00:34:32,612 --> 00:34:36,531
I wonder if they would've
ended up together if they'd had more time.

600
00:34:36,532 --> 00:34:40,994
If their story does keep going, we'd love
to see them as a couple, wouldn't we?

601
00:34:40,995 --> 00:34:42,788
Definitely. Right.

602
00:34:42,789 --> 00:34:46,291
I think Bo chose words
he felt would embarrass her the least.

603
00:34:46,292 --> 00:34:48,543
- "I like someone else."
- He kept it nice and short.

604
00:34:48,544 --> 00:34:49,420
"I've decided."

605
00:34:52,840 --> 00:34:54,217
<i>Next up is…</i>

606
00:34:55,927 --> 00:34:57,135
<i>Ari.</i>

607
00:34:57,136 --> 00:34:58,096
Yeah!

608
00:34:59,430 --> 00:35:01,015
Sorry, brothers. I'm going first.

609
00:35:01,849 --> 00:35:03,434
- Go for it.
- All right.

610
00:35:11,442 --> 00:35:13,986
First of all, out in the real world,

611
00:35:14,654 --> 00:35:17,447
you don't get many chances
to express your feelings,

612
00:35:17,448 --> 00:35:20,408
and in my experience,
many people can be cold.

613
00:35:20,409 --> 00:35:24,956
But everyone here
tried their best to welcome each other

614
00:35:26,374 --> 00:35:27,875
and face each other head-on.

615
00:35:29,001 --> 00:35:32,463
A lot of my old perspectives
got turned upside down in a good way.

616
00:35:33,422 --> 00:35:37,300
Thanks to all of you, I've grown so much.
Seriously, thank you!

617
00:35:37,301 --> 00:35:38,678
Thank you.

618
00:35:39,720 --> 00:35:41,597
- <i>That's so sweet.</i>
- Thanks, Ari.

619
00:35:45,184 --> 00:35:48,312
So now, during our time here at school,

620
00:35:49,147 --> 00:35:50,064
I've…

621
00:35:52,275 --> 00:35:53,442
fallen for a woman.

622
00:35:54,193 --> 00:35:55,069
And that is…

623
00:35:56,195 --> 00:35:57,238
Hikaru!

624
00:35:59,574 --> 00:36:01,616
Come on up.

625
00:36:01,617 --> 00:36:02,577
Okay.

626
00:36:10,168 --> 00:36:11,294
- Wassup.
- Hey.

627
00:36:17,008 --> 00:36:18,217
<i>What's gonna happen?</i>

628
00:36:20,678 --> 00:36:22,555
I object!

629
00:36:23,347 --> 00:36:24,640
<i>Ohhh.</i>

630
00:36:34,400 --> 00:36:35,234
<i>Just them?</i>

631
00:36:38,487 --> 00:36:40,698
All right. Then let me go first.

632
00:36:47,038 --> 00:36:47,955
When I got here,

633
00:36:49,123 --> 00:36:51,917
you were the very first person
who caught my eye.

634
00:36:51,918 --> 00:36:53,084
I was like, "Whoa!"

635
00:36:53,085 --> 00:36:55,086
You were the first one
I was interested in,

636
00:36:55,087 --> 00:36:56,880
and we're from the same prefecture.

637
00:36:56,881 --> 00:37:00,133
Well, you're exactly my type,
with the blonde hair and snaggletooth.

638
00:37:00,134 --> 00:37:01,219
I thought, "That's her."

639
00:37:01,844 --> 00:37:05,765
So, yeah, something eventually
just clicked for me. I got hooked.

640
00:37:07,308 --> 00:37:10,310
And along the way,
as we spent time together,

641
00:37:10,311 --> 00:37:11,729
I saw the way you…

642
00:37:12,813 --> 00:37:15,732
thought things through
and took time with decisions.

643
00:37:15,733 --> 00:37:16,567
At first,

644
00:37:17,568 --> 00:37:20,946
I thought maybe you were indecisive
about your feelings.

645
00:37:20,947 --> 00:37:24,241
But once I decided to give
that side of you a chance

646
00:37:24,242 --> 00:37:26,618
and got to know you as a full person,

647
00:37:26,619 --> 00:37:28,120
I realized that was actually…

648
00:37:29,872 --> 00:37:31,457
exactly what I was looking for.

649
00:37:33,042 --> 00:37:34,793
Even that cautious side of you

650
00:37:34,794 --> 00:37:38,547
started to look super lovable
as we spent time here together.

651
00:37:39,632 --> 00:37:41,299
And then, gradually,

652
00:37:41,300 --> 00:37:43,970
my feelings for you
just grew bigger and bigger.

653
00:37:45,763 --> 00:37:48,807
Even when we weren't together,
I couldn't stop thinking about you.

654
00:37:48,808 --> 00:37:49,850
Literally, nonstop.

655
00:37:50,476 --> 00:37:54,897
Yeah. And then I realized, "You know what,
Ari, you must really like her."

656
00:37:56,315 --> 00:37:59,026
I wanted you
to experience true love with me.

657
00:38:00,069 --> 00:38:03,864
I want to be the last boyfriend
you'll ever have in your life.

658
00:38:05,074 --> 00:38:07,243
I swear I'll make you happy.

659
00:38:07,910 --> 00:38:10,204
I hope you'll trust me
and want to be with me.

660
00:38:10,871 --> 00:38:12,832
I'd love to live in Kanagawa together.

661
00:38:26,512 --> 00:38:28,513
It's short, but let me read this aloud.

662
00:38:28,514 --> 00:38:29,473
Okay.

663
00:38:34,186 --> 00:38:35,896
Um, "Dear Hikaru,

664
00:38:37,189 --> 00:38:39,065
since I first told you how I felt,

665
00:38:39,066 --> 00:38:42,695
this is my first proper letter to you,
apart from the one on Valentine's Day."

666
00:38:44,030 --> 00:38:47,157
"Even after turning me down, thank you
for taking my feelings seriously

667
00:38:47,158 --> 00:38:48,868
when I said I didn't want regrets."

668
00:38:50,578 --> 00:38:53,371
"I've always heard it said
that seeing someone without makeup

669
00:38:53,372 --> 00:38:54,707
<i>will reveal your true feelings,</i>

670
00:38:56,167 --> 00:38:57,668
<i>and for me, that moment alone</i>

671
00:38:59,170 --> 00:39:01,797
was more than enough reason
to be attracted to you."

672
00:39:03,090 --> 00:39:04,467
"When I think about the future,

673
00:39:05,092 --> 00:39:06,969
I can picture a bright one with you."

674
00:39:08,179 --> 00:39:11,390
"And as you opened up to me,
I found myself liking you even more."

675
00:39:12,433 --> 00:39:15,518
"I promise to make you happy,
which is why I ask

676
00:39:15,519 --> 00:39:16,729
that you go out with me."

677
00:39:17,980 --> 00:39:19,857
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

678
00:39:24,111 --> 00:39:25,237
Mm…

679
00:39:28,991 --> 00:39:29,950
Mm…

680
00:39:31,827 --> 00:39:33,287
Well, Bo,

681
00:39:34,205 --> 00:39:36,290
you show subtle acts of kindness.

682
00:39:37,166 --> 00:39:39,251
Like, mm…

683
00:39:40,127 --> 00:39:42,712
Like when you carry my bag
before I even notice

684
00:39:42,713 --> 00:39:44,173
- because I always forget it.
- Hmm.

685
00:39:44,840 --> 00:39:47,467
I think you're a really great guy.

686
00:39:47,468 --> 00:39:48,636
Mmm.

687
00:39:52,181 --> 00:39:53,516
But…

688
00:39:56,143 --> 00:39:56,977
mm…

689
00:40:04,402 --> 00:40:07,071
I wasn't able to fall in love with you.

690
00:40:11,325 --> 00:40:12,743
I understand. Thank you.

691
00:40:20,960 --> 00:40:21,836
Ari.

692
00:40:22,753 --> 00:40:23,796
From day one,

693
00:40:24,880 --> 00:40:28,384
you were, you know,
almost annoyingly telling me all day long.

694
00:40:29,009 --> 00:40:33,139
You know, I was like, "Are you gonna be
rhyming and rapping the whole time?"

695
00:40:33,639 --> 00:40:36,934
You were always expressing
how you felt about me.

696
00:40:37,435 --> 00:40:38,769
Mmm.

697
00:40:40,938 --> 00:40:42,565
And it really got through to me.

698
00:40:45,443 --> 00:40:48,779
I honestly felt so much love from you.

699
00:40:50,197 --> 00:40:51,031
Mm…

700
00:40:52,074 --> 00:40:54,326
And it's meant more than I can say.

701
00:41:08,507 --> 00:41:10,342
Let's go back to Kanagawa together.

702
00:41:12,803 --> 00:41:13,971
Aah, yes!

703
00:41:17,141 --> 00:41:18,601
Hikaru!

704
00:41:19,101 --> 00:41:21,436
<i>Whoo!</i>

705
00:41:21,437 --> 00:41:22,854
<i>Kisses!</i>

706
00:41:22,855 --> 00:41:24,898
She's dying! She's dying!

707
00:41:24,899 --> 00:41:27,650
- My headpiece's gonna come off.
- Oh, sorry, sorry, sorry.

708
00:41:27,651 --> 00:41:30,653
Sorry, brothers. I'm outta here.

709
00:41:30,654 --> 00:41:31,988
- Congrats.
- Thanks, man.

710
00:41:31,989 --> 00:41:33,031
Congrats, Ari.

711
00:41:33,032 --> 00:41:35,075
I seriously thought
I was gonna get rejected.

712
00:41:36,202 --> 00:41:38,329
- Seriously, you're the best.
- Let's go!

713
00:41:39,371 --> 00:41:40,915
I really thought I was done.

714
00:41:46,837 --> 00:41:48,380
Viva wassup!

715
00:41:49,507 --> 00:41:51,550
That guy…

716
00:41:54,011 --> 00:41:55,304
<i>Next up is…</i>

717
00:41:56,222 --> 00:41:57,389
<i>Maririn.</i>

718
00:42:00,392 --> 00:42:01,559
- Okay.
- Good luck.

719
00:42:01,560 --> 00:42:02,937
I'll do my best.

720
00:42:14,490 --> 00:42:15,908
Um…

721
00:42:16,784 --> 00:42:19,870
Listening to everyone's confessions,
I'm already about to cry.

722
00:42:20,412 --> 00:42:22,497
But I'll do my best and confess too.

723
00:42:22,498 --> 00:42:24,792
First of all, um…

724
00:42:28,837 --> 00:42:30,838
At first, I was surprised

725
00:42:30,839 --> 00:42:33,676
that it would be so scary
to face reality like this.

726
00:42:35,594 --> 00:42:37,513
I couldn't really open up,

727
00:42:38,222 --> 00:42:41,099
and it took me way too long
to tell you about myself

728
00:42:41,100 --> 00:42:42,768
or to get close to you all.

729
00:42:45,187 --> 00:42:47,356
This was the first time
I had a home-cooked meal.

730
00:42:48,148 --> 00:42:50,150
I'd never sat around a table

731
00:42:51,235 --> 00:42:53,779
and eaten with people,
like a family, before.

732
00:42:54,989 --> 00:42:55,906
Like…

733
00:42:56,824 --> 00:42:58,866
you all looked me straight in the eye

734
00:42:58,867 --> 00:43:02,121
and kept trying to understand me,
even when I stayed insecure.

735
00:43:04,790 --> 00:43:06,709
You really listened to me so much.

736
00:43:07,293 --> 00:43:08,127
So, thank you.

737
00:43:11,547 --> 00:43:15,342
I still have a lot to work on,
but I feel like I've become stronger.

738
00:43:17,428 --> 00:43:20,306
And the person I want to confess
my feelings to is Tai-chan.

739
00:43:21,473 --> 00:43:22,975
- All right.
- Please come up.

740
00:43:46,790 --> 00:43:49,710
I chose you based on my first impression,

741
00:43:51,086 --> 00:43:53,380
but I heard that you had feelings
for someone else,

742
00:43:54,006 --> 00:43:55,424
so I gave you up.

743
00:43:56,383 --> 00:44:00,638
But as we talked more and more,
I got to know your kindness,

744
00:44:01,680 --> 00:44:05,768
and the way you were so natural around me
really got through to me.

745
00:44:07,436 --> 00:44:10,105
I think I already know how you feel,

746
00:44:10,981 --> 00:44:13,609
but I wanted to say it
so I wouldn't have any regrets.

747
00:44:15,194 --> 00:44:16,153
Um, well…

748
00:44:18,947 --> 00:44:19,782
Um…

749
00:44:22,076 --> 00:44:25,204
This is who I am,
so if you're okay with someone like me…

750
00:44:27,956 --> 00:44:30,209
um, yeah, please go out with me.

751
00:44:38,300 --> 00:44:40,094
Well, first of all, I want to say,

752
00:44:41,553 --> 00:44:43,347
you faced me head-on the whole time.

753
00:44:43,972 --> 00:44:44,973
Thanks for that.

754
00:44:46,600 --> 00:44:50,896
And, well, you were always so honest
and earnest in expressing your emotions,

755
00:44:51,814 --> 00:44:53,273
and your feelings toward me.

756
00:44:54,650 --> 00:44:56,402
I took them to heart.

757
00:44:57,194 --> 00:44:58,362
But having said that,

758
00:44:59,571 --> 00:45:01,031
I don't wanna give up on my own.

759
00:45:01,824 --> 00:45:04,118
And there's still someone
I can't give up on.

760
00:45:07,204 --> 00:45:10,249
So thank you for your honesty,
but right now,

761
00:45:11,291 --> 00:45:12,543
I can't reciprocate.

762
00:45:14,169 --> 00:45:17,631
I'm sorry. But thank you
for facing me head-on. Thank you.

763
00:45:20,884 --> 00:45:22,636
Thank you for listening to me.

764
00:45:24,346 --> 00:45:26,223
- Let's do our best.
- Yeah, good luck.

765
00:45:27,057 --> 00:45:28,474
- Don't make her cry.
- No.

766
00:45:28,475 --> 00:45:30,894
- <i>Wow, that was really nice.</i>
- <i>Aw!</i>

767
00:45:36,608 --> 00:45:37,942
- Well done.
- Your hand is so sweaty.

768
00:45:37,943 --> 00:45:39,318
- Are you good?
- Yeah, I'm good.

769
00:45:39,319 --> 00:45:41,612
- <i>She's so kind.</i>
- <i>That's friendship.</i>

770
00:45:41,613 --> 00:45:42,823
<i>Next up is…</i>

771
00:45:44,116 --> 00:45:45,159
<i>Kazu-kun.</i>

772
00:45:47,202 --> 00:45:48,287
All right.

773
00:45:57,671 --> 00:45:59,798
First of all, in the end,

774
00:46:00,841 --> 00:46:02,509
this experience turned out to be…

775
00:46:03,510 --> 00:46:05,095
a truly precious…

776
00:46:06,221 --> 00:46:08,307
and irreplaceable treasure to me.

777
00:46:09,683 --> 00:46:13,102
I never thought I would grow
as a person at my age.

778
00:46:13,103 --> 00:46:15,813
I never thought I'd discover
a new side of myself.

779
00:46:15,814 --> 00:46:17,483
That's thanks to all of you.

780
00:46:19,067 --> 00:46:19,985
So, thanks, everyone.

781
00:46:23,864 --> 00:46:26,533
The person I want to confess
my feelings to is…

782
00:46:28,118 --> 00:46:28,952
Ruru.

783
00:46:31,121 --> 00:46:31,955
Yes.

784
00:46:33,165 --> 00:46:34,833
- Good luck.
- Here I go.

785
00:46:45,177 --> 00:46:46,428
Hold on a second.

786
00:46:47,971 --> 00:46:50,348
- <i>This is no surprise.</i>
- <i>Yeah.</i>

787
00:46:50,349 --> 00:46:52,392
<i>Leo's been devoted to her this whole time.</i>

788
00:47:00,901 --> 00:47:02,361
Kazuma, Leo,

789
00:47:03,362 --> 00:47:04,404
let me jump in.

790
00:47:14,623 --> 00:47:15,457
I'll go first.

791
00:47:17,334 --> 00:47:20,587
First of all, compared to everyone else…

792
00:47:22,589 --> 00:47:25,425
we didn't have as much time
to spend with each other.

793
00:47:26,093 --> 00:47:29,680
But the time I spent with you
was the most intense. Truly.

794
00:47:31,932 --> 00:47:36,395
Before I knew it, I'd fallen for you,
even with just the little time we'd had.

795
00:47:40,357 --> 00:47:42,276
After today's graduation ceremony,

796
00:47:43,235 --> 00:47:45,237
we're going back to our ordinary lives.

797
00:47:46,822 --> 00:47:48,031
I wanna say…

798
00:47:50,576 --> 00:47:51,952
even after we go back,

799
00:47:53,161 --> 00:47:55,664
I want to be the one closest
to you, supporting you.

800
00:47:58,709 --> 00:48:00,627
Going to a sauna with the girl I like…

801
00:48:03,338 --> 00:48:05,799
<i>making Valentine's chocolates
and giving them to her…</i>

802
00:48:08,927 --> 00:48:10,761
Looking that person in the eye

803
00:48:10,762 --> 00:48:14,182
and telling her how I feel
in front of everyone like this…

804
00:48:15,434 --> 00:48:16,810
I'd never done any of that.

805
00:48:18,979 --> 00:48:20,022
You should know…

806
00:48:21,440 --> 00:48:23,609
you've claimed so many of my firsts.

807
00:48:24,860 --> 00:48:26,778
It's only right you come home with me.

808
00:48:28,322 --> 00:48:29,823
Ruru, I like you a lot.

809
00:48:39,249 --> 00:48:40,334
All right.

810
00:48:41,752 --> 00:48:44,504
Well, um, at first,

811
00:48:45,839 --> 00:48:48,759
I spent a lot of time worrying
and second-guessing myself.

812
00:48:49,676 --> 00:48:50,510
Mmm.

813
00:48:52,012 --> 00:48:56,141
Honestly, there were times when I thought
finding romance wasn't all that fun,

814
00:48:57,517 --> 00:49:01,605
but being here and watching everyone
approach love so sincerely,

815
00:49:02,522 --> 00:49:03,982
made me want to do that too.

816
00:49:06,109 --> 00:49:07,444
You've turned me down before,

817
00:49:08,403 --> 00:49:11,323
but I felt I still didn't want
to give you up.

818
00:49:12,282 --> 00:49:14,660
I don't want to end it here,

819
00:49:15,327 --> 00:49:18,038
but I do want to see
what lies ahead of us.

820
00:49:19,790 --> 00:49:22,042
I want you, Ruru, to go out with me.

821
00:49:30,300 --> 00:49:35,013
Well, I should begin by saying
you caught my attention from the start.

822
00:49:35,931 --> 00:49:37,975
You were always great company,

823
00:49:38,934 --> 00:49:41,478
and before I knew it,
I was falling for you.

824
00:49:46,066 --> 00:49:48,193
And then, after your date,

825
00:49:49,569 --> 00:49:51,113
<i>you told me what happened at the villa.</i>

826
00:49:51,822 --> 00:49:53,448
<i>You were honest with me.</i>

827
00:49:54,866 --> 00:49:55,701
Even so,

828
00:49:56,994 --> 00:50:01,288
I still believe that nobody feels
more strongly about you than I do.

829
00:50:01,289 --> 00:50:02,332
No one can.

830
00:50:04,751 --> 00:50:05,961
So, out of everything,

831
00:50:07,045 --> 00:50:08,797
that's what I would tell you, Ruru.

832
00:50:11,258 --> 00:50:12,968
I've never been sure about anyone.

833
00:50:14,302 --> 00:50:15,429
I know it's you, Ruru.

834
00:50:16,263 --> 00:50:17,889
It is. And when I leave,

835
00:50:18,682 --> 00:50:19,933
I want you with me.

836
00:50:30,193 --> 00:50:31,820
So, first, Tai-chan.

837
00:50:33,530 --> 00:50:34,489
With you…

838
00:50:35,657 --> 00:50:39,202
I was usually the one who was
always dumping my feelings onto you.

839
00:50:39,703 --> 00:50:42,122
<i>And, every…</i>

840
00:50:42,789 --> 00:50:44,624
<i>every time we talked,</i>

841
00:50:45,751 --> 00:50:49,546
<i>you would say to me,
"Talking with you has changed me."</i>

842
00:50:50,380 --> 00:50:52,799
No matter who
you're talking with, Tai-chan,

843
00:50:53,425 --> 00:50:56,385
you're always able
to express your gratitude

844
00:50:56,386 --> 00:50:57,929
and apologize when you need to.

845
00:50:59,848 --> 00:51:02,768
I think that's one of the best things
I learned from you.

846
00:51:03,435 --> 00:51:04,269
But…

847
00:51:05,937 --> 00:51:10,734
